<title>UK: T&amp;N drops after SBC Warburg downgrade.</title>
<headline>T&amp;N drops after SBC Warburg downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in T&amp;N Plc fell on Wednesday after analysts at SBC Warburg cut their recommendation on the stock to &quot;sell&quot; from &quot;hold&quot;, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1450 GMT, T&amp;N shares were 8-1/2p weaker at 171-1/2 on volume of 5.4 million.</p>
<p>&quot;Warburg's downgraded to sell and that's put it under a bit of pressure,&quot; one market-maker said.</p>
<p>Analysts at SBC Warburg were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
